    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d125">

                <pb facs="0256" n="238" sameAs="frus:frus1946v01/pg238"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BB/11–2246: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Senator Austin </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-11-22T19:00:00-05:00">November 22,
                            1946—7 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>293. For Gadel. Our reasons for preferring Netherlands to Byelorussia as
                    candidate for ECOSOC are set out below for your consideration when subject is
                    next discussed by Secretary and USDel: (1) Among remaining candidates for
                    three-year membership on ECOSOC, Netherlands is only state willing and able to
                    collaborate wholeheartedly in creation and implementation of ITO, in our view,
                    most important tasks to be undertaken by ECOSOC. (2) Netherlands has
                    demonstrated unswerving fidelity to western democratic principles in all organs
                    UN and Van Kleffens has made particularly notable contribution to work of SC. In
                    view this record, failure of US to support Netherlands might have adverse
                    reaction not only upon Netherlands but upon other small western European states
                    as well.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
